    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72103" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδό-ω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lead by the right way,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὗτός σ᾽ ὁδώσει τὴν τρίγωνον ἐς
					χθόνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					813
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυστέκμαρτον ἐς τέχνην ὥδωσα
				θνητούς</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				498
			</span></i> : c. inf., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν φρονεῖν
				βροτοὺς ὁδώσαντα</span>
			<i>who put</i> mortals <i>on the way</i> to wisdom, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				176
			</span></i> (lyr.); of things, <i>direct, ordain,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ion</u>
				1050
			</span></i> (lyr.):—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be on the right way,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἀπ᾽ ὑμέων χρηστῶς ὁδοῦται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					4.139
				</span></i>
			.</div>
